The '''1974 Oklahoma Sooners football team''' represented the University of
Oklahoma in the 1974 NCAA Division I football season. Playing under a bowl
and television ban imposed by NCAA probation, the Sooners went undefeated
and were later voted national champions by the AP poll once Alabama lost
its bowl game.

Rod Shoate and Joe Washington were named consensus All-Americans.

